================================================================================
Machine-learned models
================================================================================

No third-party model weights are distributed with mac4DSTEM. The stock
Ultralytics `yolov8n.mlpackage` (AGPL-3.0) that was added to the Xcode project
on 2026-09-05 as a reference was never part of a shipped build and was removed
from the tree on 2026-09-07. abTEM (GPL-3.0) is used only as a simulation tool
during development; nothing from it is distributed. Any detector mac4DSTEM
ships is trained on its own data with its own weights.


================================================================================
Third-party method
================================================================================

The phase-mapping matcher (DiffractoKit's DiffractoOrientation/PhaseVectorMatching.swift, which the app links; see
the DiffractoKit section above) implements the vector-matching method and, as `.knownVariants`, the per-position decision rule with its two constants
(at most one surviving vector → the matrix; a residual cutoff of 0.07 Å⁻¹) described in
Thronsen et al., "Scanning precession electron diffraction data analysis approaches for phase
mapping of precipitates in aluminium alloys", Ultramicroscopy 255 (2024) 113861, licensed
CC BY 4.0 (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/). No code from the authors' repository
(which carries no licence) is copied.

